$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------
$ Reference case: marina_lay2
$ 2D horizontal, 2 vertical layers, non-hydrostatic (Keller-box), explicit
$ time integration.  This is the SwashExpLay2DHflow path targeted by the
$ GPU port.  JONSWAP waves enter from the west, a sponge absorbs at the east.
$ Domain 200 m x 150 m at 1 m resolution; 60 s of simulation.
$ ------------------------------------------------------------------------
PROJECT 'marina' '01'
    'GPU regression: layered non-hydrostatic marina'
    'physics reference for SwashExpLay2DHflow'
    'generated by tests/cases/gen_inputs.py'
$
$ fixed seed keeps the random JONSWAP phases reproducible between runs
SET LEVEL 0. DEPMIN 0.001 MAXERR 3 SEED 12345 CARTESIAN
MODE DYNAMIC TWODIMENSIONAL
COORDINATES CARTESIAN
$
CGRID REGULAR 0. 0. 0. 200. 150. 200 150
VERTICAL 2
$
INPGRID BOTTOM REGULAR 0. 0. 0. 200 150 1. 1.
READINP BOTTOM 1. 'bot.dat' 3 0 FREE
$
INITIAL ZERO
$
BOUND SHAPESPEC JONSWAP 3.3 SIG PEAK DSPR DEGREES
BOUNDCOND SIDE W CCW BTYPE WEAKREFL SMOOTHING 10 SEC CON SPECTRUM 0.8 6.0 0. 20. 600 SEC
SPONGELAYER E 30.
$
NONHYDROSTATIC BOX 1.0 PREC ILUD
BREAKING 0.6 0.3
FRICTION MANNING 0.019
TIMEI METHOD EXPLICIT 0.4 0.8
$
$ --- output: full-field water level and velocities every 0.5 s, gauges at 20 Hz
POINTS 'GAUGES' 40. 75. 80. 75. 120. 75. 160. 75. 100. 40.
TABLE 'GAUGES' NOHEAD 'gauges.tbl' TSEC WATL OUTPUT 000000.000 0.05 SEC
BLOCK 'COMPGRID' NOHEAD 'fields.mat' LAY 3 BOTL WATL VEL VELK OUTPUT 000000.000 0.5 SEC
$
TEST 1 0
COMPUTE 000000.000 0.02 SEC 000100.000
STOP
